---
import '../../../styles/global.css';
import ParadigmShift from './ParadigmShift.astro';
import './styles.css';

const createCommand = 'npx --yes @hairness/cli@latest create my-home';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="UTF-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
		<meta
			name="description"
			content="A local iteration of the Hairness Home-first landing."
		/>
		<title>Hairness — Home-first system</title>
	</head>
	<body class="v3-body">
		<div class="v3-labbar">
			<a href="/lab/">← Iterations</a>
			<span>003 · Home-first system</span>
			<strong>Local only</strong>
		</div>

		<div class="v3-page">
			<header class="v3-header">
				<a class="v3-brand" href="#top" aria-label="Hairness home">
					<i aria-hidden="true"></i>
					hairness
				</a>
				<nav aria-label="Main navigation">
					<a href="#shift">Paradigm</a>
					<a href="#model">Mental model</a>
					<a href="#collaboration">Collaboration</a>
				</nav>
				<a class="v3-header-cta" href="#start">Create your Home</a>
			</header>

			<main id="top">
				<section class="v3-hero">
					<p class="v3-eyebrow">The Home-first framework for agentic work.</p>
					<h1>Your agentic stack already exists. <em>Give it a Home.</em></h1>
					<p class="v3-lede">
						Hairness is an open, Home-first framework for building a
						source-owned human-agent work environment around the providers,
						repositories, and agentic tools you already use.
					</p>
					<div class="v3-actions">
						<a class="v3-button v3-button-primary" href="#shift">See the Home-first shift</a>
						<a class="v3-button v3-button-secondary" href="#start">Create your Home</a>
					</div>
					<p class="v3-proof">
						<span>Open source</span>
						<i>·</i>
						<span>Codex + Claude today</span>
						<i>·</i>
						<span>Hairness 0.5 alpha</span>
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="v3-statement">
					<p>
						Agents are a new way of working.
						<strong>They need a new organizing paradigm.</strong>
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="v3-section v3-shift-section" id="shift">
					<header class="v3-section-header">
						<div>
							<p class="v3-section-index">01 / The paradigm shift</p>
							<h2>Keep the system. Change what owns it.</h2>
						</div>
						<p>
							Target-first turns repositories into accidental agent Homes.
							Home-first reorganizes the same system around explicit ownership.
						</p>
					</header>
					<ParadigmShift />
					<p class="v3-pullquote">
						Hairness doesn’t replace your agentic stack.
						<strong>It gives it a Home.</strong>
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="v3-section v3-model-section" id="model">
					<header class="v3-section-header">
						<div>
							<p class="v3-section-index">02 / The mental model</p>
							<h2>Home-first changes how you see the system.</h2>
						</div>
						<p>
							The existing vocabulary describes delivery formats. Hairness
							adds the ownership and lifecycle abstractions above them.
						</p>
					</header>

					<div class="v3-shifts" aria-label="Home-first mental model shifts">
						<article>
							<span>01</span>
							<p><small>Format</small><strong>Skill</strong></p>
							<i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
							<div>
								<small>Ownership</small>
								<strong>Agentic Asset</strong>
								<p>A Skill describes invocation. An Asset defines the reusable source you own.</p>
							</div>
						</article>
						<article>
							<span>02</span>
							<p><small>Ephemeral result</small><strong>Output</strong></p>
							<i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
							<div>
								<small>Durable product of work</small>
								<strong>Artifact</strong>
								<p>Evidence gains provenance, a lifecycle and an explicit owner.</p>
							</div>
						</article>
						<article>
							<span>03</span>
							<p><small>Accidental center</small><strong>Repository</strong></p>
							<i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
							<div>
								<small>Independent destination</small>
								<strong>Target</strong>
								<p>The product keeps its own code, history and delivery. A Binding reaches it.</p>
							</div>
						</article>
						<article>
							<span>04</span>
							<p><small>Temporary continuity</small><strong>Session</strong></p>
							<i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
							<div>
								<small>Owned collaboration</small>
								<strong>Home + Desk</strong>
								<p>Shared canon and private working continuity have distinct owners.</p>
							</div>
						</article>
					</div>

					<figure class="v3-lifecycle" aria-labelledby="lifecycle-title">
						<figcaption>
							<p class="v3-section-index">The Asset / Artifact lifecycle</p>
							<h3 id="lifecycle-title">Products for work become products of work.</h3>
						</figcaption>
						<div class="v3-lifecycle-flow">
							<div class="v3-flow-node v3-flow-asset">
								<small>Reusable source</small>
								<strong>Asset</strong>
								<span>product for work</span>
							</div>
							<i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
							<div class="v3-flow-step">
								<small>Provider projection</small>
								<strong>Skill · command · agent surface</strong>
							</div>
							<i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
							<div class="v3-flow-node v3-flow-artifact">
								<small>Evidence returns</small>
								<strong>Artifact</strong>
								<span>product of work</span>
							</div>
							<i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
							<div class="v3-flow-step v3-flow-human">
								<small>Explicit gate</small>
								<strong>Human judgment</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
						<p class="v3-return-line">
							<span>keep as evidence</span>
							<strong>promote into a new or better Asset</strong>
						</p>
					</figure>
				</section>

				<section class="v3-section v3-collab-section" id="collaboration">
					<header class="v3-section-header">
						<div>
							<p class="v3-section-index">03 / Human-agent collaboration</p>
							<h2>Share the Home. Keep a Desk of your own.</h2>
						</div>
						<p>
							The Home holds what the collaboration should inherit. The Desk
							holds what you and your agents are still working through.
						</p>
					</header>

					<div class="v3-collab-map">
						<aside class="v3-provider-note">
							<small>Replaceable entry</small>
							<strong>Agent session</strong>
							<span>Codex · Claude</span>
						</aside>

						<section class="v3-home-boundary">
							<header>
								<div>
									<small>SHARED, SOURCE-OWNED CANON</small>
									<strong>Home</strong>
								</div>
								<span>Assets · conventions · accepted work</span>
							</header>
							<div class="v3-desk-surface">
								<div>
									<small>PRIVATE CONTINUITY</small>
									<strong>Your Desk</strong>
								</div>
								<p>
									<span>drafts</span>
									<span>working Artifacts</span>
									<span>local Bindings</span>
								</p>
							</div>
						</section>

						<aside class="v3-target-note">
							<small>Reached through a Binding</small>
							<strong>Independent Target</strong>
							<span>code · history · delivery</span>
						</aside>
					</div>

					<div class="v3-collab-sequence" aria-label="Human-agent collaboration lifecycle">
						<span>Equip</span><i>→</i>
						<span>Enter</span><i>→</i>
						<span>Reach Target</span><i>→</i>
						<span>Return Artifact</span><i>→</i>
						<strong>Human curation</strong>
					</div>
				</section>

				<section class="v3-authority">
					<header>
						<p class="v3-section-index">04 / Clear authority</p>
						<h2>Hairness can be the center without running everything.</h2>
					</header>
					<div class="v3-authority-flow">
						<div>
							<small>Providers</small>
							<strong>Execute</strong>
							<p>host sessions<br />connect services<br />run capabilities</p>
						</div>
						<i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
						<div class="v3-authority-home">
							<small>Hairness Home</small>
							<strong>Owns</strong>
							<p>composition<br />business Assets<br />continuity</p>
						</div>
						<i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
						<div>
							<small>Targets</small>
							<strong>Deliver</strong>
							<p>products<br />history<br />delivery</p>
						</div>
					</div>
					<p class="v3-authority-note">
						Generic integrations can remain Provider-managed. The Home owns
						the domain Assets that make your way of working yours.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="v3-section v3-homes-section">
					<header class="v3-section-header">
						<div>
							<p class="v3-section-index">05 / The new unit of adoption</p>
							<h2>Adopt an environment, not a pile of Skills.</h2>
						</div>
						<p>
							A Home can encode how a domain approaches work—not only which
							commands happen to be installed.
						</p>
					</header>

					<div class="v3-home-concept">
						<nav aria-label="Conceptual specialized Homes">
							<span>Game Development</span>
							<span>Design</span>
							<span>Research</span>
						</nav>
						<div>
							<p>Concept · Not installable yet</p>
							<strong>A Home built for the work.</strong>
							<ul>
								<li>domain Assets</li>
								<li>working conventions</li>
								<li>meaningful Artifacts</li>
								<li>independent Targets</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>

					<p class="v3-home-question">
						If your agents had a Home,
						<em>what would yours be built for?</em>
					</p>
				</section>

				<section class="v3-start" id="start">
					<div>
						<p class="v3-section-index">Hairness 0.5 alpha</p>
						<h2>The paradigm already runs.</h2>
						<p>
							Create a source-owned Home with a Desk, Assets, Artifacts,
							Bindings and independent Targets. Use Codex and Claude today.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="v3-terminal">
						<header><span></span><span></span><span></span><small>create a Home</small></header>
						<code>{createCommand}</code>
						<button type="button" data-v3-copy={createCommand}>Copy</button>
					</div>
					<footer>
						<a class="v3-button v3-button-light" href="https://github.com/thevzion/hairness">
							View Hairness on GitHub ↗
						</a>
						<a href="/home-first/">Read the technical docs →</a>
					</footer>
					<small>
						Open framework · Specialized Homes are still conceptual · Broader
						integrations remain future work
					</small>
				</section>
			</main>

			<footer class="v3-footer">
				<a class="v3-brand" href="#top"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>hairness</a>
				<p>Own the place where humans and agents build what comes next.</p>
				<a href="/lab/">Iteration lab</a>
			</footer>
		</div>

		<script>
			const copyButton =
				document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-v3-copy]');

			copyButton?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
				const command = copyButton.dataset.v3Copy;
				if (!command || !navigator.clipboard) return;
				await navigator.clipboard.writeText(command);
				copyButton.textContent = 'Copied';
				window.setTimeout(() => {
					copyButton.textContent = 'Copy';
				}, 1400);
			});
		</script>
	</body>
</html>
